[TEST 1] Multi-column index with range condition and function-based ORDER BY -> verify ORDER BY skip using index order     

===================================================
col_a    col_b    
50     200     
30     300     

Query plan:
iscan
    class: tbl_orderby_num node[?]
    index: idx_col_a_upper_col_b term[?]
    sargs: term[?]
    sort:  ? desc, ? desc
    cost:  ? card ?
Query stmt:
select tbl_orderby_num.col_a, tbl_orderby_num.col_b,  upper( cast(tbl_orderby_num.col_b as varchar)) from tbl_orderby_num tbl_orderby_num where (tbl_orderby_num.col_a> ?:? ) and  upper( cast(tbl_orderby_num.col_b as varchar))> cast('?' as varchar) order by ? desc , ? desc  for orderby_num() between  ?:?  and  ?:? 
/* ---> skip ORDER BY */
===================================================
    
[TEST 1.1] Function expression mismatch in ORDER BY -> should NOT skip order by     

===================================================
col_a    col_b    
1     300     
1     200     
1     100     

Query plan:
temp(order by)
    subplan: iscan
                 class: tbl_orderby_num node[?]
                 index: idx_col_a_upper_col_b term[?] AND term[?]
                 cost:  ? card ?
    sort:  ? desc
    cost:  ? card ?
Query stmt:
select tbl_orderby_num.col_a, tbl_orderby_num.col_b,  upper( cast(tbl_orderby_num.col_b as varchar)|| cast('_' as varchar)) from tbl_orderby_num tbl_orderby_num where  upper( cast(tbl_orderby_num.col_b as varchar))> cast('?' as varchar) and tbl_orderby_num.col_a= ?:?  order by ? desc 
